# Thespian's Stage becomes a copy of Dark Depths. Counters are not copied and the Stage doesn't enter, so "enters with ten ice
# counters" doesn't apply (CR 707.2; the ruling): it is a Dark Depths with no ice counters. Bot1 then controls two legendary
# Dark Depths, and the legend rule puts the one Bot1 doesn't keep into the graveyard (CR 704.5j): Bot1 keeps the Stage. Its
# state trigger (CR 603.8) sacrifices it and makes Marit Lage, a legendary 20/20 flying, indestructible Avatar. Both lands
# end in the graveyard, the real Dark Depths still unused with its ten ice counters gone with it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Dark Depths
Mox Pearl
Sol Ring
Thespian's Stage
Forest x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Dark Depths.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Thespian's Stage.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Thespian's Stage.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Dark Depths; Ability: becomes)
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Dark Depths#2)
? Bot1.Graveyard = Dark Depths
? Bot1.Battlefield.Dark Depths.Counters.Ice = (absent)
? Stack = Dark Depths
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Pearl; Sol Ring; Marit Lage
Bot1.Battlefield.Marit Lage.Power = 20
Bot1.Battlefield.Marit Lage.Keywords = Flying; Indestructible
Bot1.Battlefield.Marit Lage.Supertypes = Legendary
Bot1.Graveyard = Thespian's Stage; Dark Depths
Stack.Count = 0
